okay so there's a hypothesis or to use  the term colloquially and not  scientifically don't yell at me there's  a theory that Joe Biden has been pulled  in to run in the 2020 Democratic primary  specifically to enable super-delegates  to decide who the nominee is in a way  that will prevent Bernie Sanders from  being the nominee now I want to be  really clear it seems every time I talk  about Joe Biden people react as if I'm  either praising him or criticizing him  we'll all I'm doing is telling you what  is being said and analyzing it so let's  discuss it to understand this theory you  need to understand how the DNC changed  its super delegate rules since the 2016  primary more and more people are  emailing me emailing me about this and  some people say David you've got to  debunk this and others say David you've  got to expose that this is what's going  on so let's see what's actually going on  and it gets a little wonky but you you  need to understand how it works in  democratic primaries you have to get 15%  of the vote to get any delegates so  imagine that there's a state with ten  delegates up for grabs and they a lot  those delegates proportionally meaning  it's not winner-take-all  you might think if I get 10% of the vote  I get 10% of the delegates meaning one  out of the ten delegates but you would  be wrong and the reason you're wrong is  that many states have a 15% minimum  required so everyone who gets under 15%  of the vote in some states gets 0  delegates whatsoever so when there's a  really crowded field you can't end up  with two candidates getting over 15% and  everybody else could conceivably split  everything that's left with no one  getting more than 15% of the vote and  what you end up with is a primary where  you might have 10 different or 12  different or 14 different candidates but  only two of the candidates actually pick  up any delegates from those states that  gets us to the discussion about  super-delegates the DNC after the 2016  Fiasco changes the rules to prevent  super-delegates from getting to decide  who is the nominee at the convention on  what's called the first ballot at the  convention there can be multiple ballots  multiple rounds of voting and the rule  was changed so that if super-delegates  would  side the outcome on the first ballot  their votes effectively aren't counted  but in the same set of rules if no  candidate gets a majority of the votes  on the first ballot  there is a second ballot and in that  second ballot the super-delegates are  allowed to vote and ultimately are  allowed to decide the outcome so what  happens when you have more and more  candidates running in 2020 is that it  becomes more and more likely that on the  first ballot nobody is going to get a  majority nobody's going to get 50% plus  one of the boat so the theory is by  adding Joe Biden an establishment  Democrat who is polling very well is  that if Biden keeps polling at 25% or if  Biden even drops the twenty percent or  two fifteen percent or even twelve  percent frankly that Biden can take  enough delegates in primaries throughout  the primary process to ensure that on  the first ballot at the Democratic  convention nobody gets that 50% plus one  that they need this leads to a second  ballot at which point all of the  super-delegates can come in and pick  somebody other than Bernie Sanders could  be Kamala Harris could be Pete Budaj  edge if he ends up being the DNC choice  it could be Biden if the ideas that  Biden will actually be the nominee so  first question is this idea  conspiratorial well conspiratorial  conspiratorial means it's suggestive of  a secret plan made by a group of people  the Democratic establishment we know has  been meeting to figure out what to do  about what they call the Bernie Sanders  problem so in that sense it's not  conspirator a rational ikan spirit  oriole but here's where I think it  doesn't make total sense which is that  you don't really need to run Biden  specifically for this reason what I mean  is running Biden so that he wins more is  kind of obvious right you you wit you  you run Biden because he has support and  he'll get more support than Bernie and  maybe he'll actually be the nominee  that's simpler and to me it's more  likely because if the plan is you run  Biden to take enough support from Bernie  so that then some other person is chosen  on the second ballot at the DNC it's  just more complicated than it needs to  be Biden is going to take some votes  from Bernie he's gonna take some votes  from Warren he's gonna take some votes  for mayor Pete and there's gonna be a  sort of thinning of the field over the  next six months before any of the  primaries actually take place that's  going to do a lot more to determine who  is ultimately the nominee then Biden's  presence would do in the second round of  voting by the time we get to the DNC so  is the DNC working towards their goal  which may be it may be to stop Bernie  Sanders of course is the idea that Biden  is a plant to give the nomination to  Kamala or Buddha judge reasonable I  don't see evidence of that right now I  think the simplest explanation if we  apply Occam's razor right Occam's razor  is normally applied to science but it  works here we shouldn't make more  assumptions than the minimum needed  should we assume Biden has been drafted  by establishment Democrats to get just  enough support that he prevents a first  ballot win by Bernie  so that then on the second ballot  super-delegates vote for Kamala Harris  well there's a much simpler explanation  which is Biden was encouraged to run by  the establishment because they liked him  more than Bernie and they want him to be  the nominee and until we have evidence  that it's much more complicated than  that  I think we shouldn't go to the more  complicated explanations if you disagree  with my analysis then please let me know
 

